# SCSS Rules

## File Structure
Each SCSS file should follow this structure:
1. Required imports
2. File header documentation
3. Variables and configuration
4. Mixins and functions
5. Base styles
6. Component styles
7. Utilities and helpers

## File Header Template
```scss
@use 'sass:math';
@use 'sass:map';
@use 'sass:list';
@use 'sass:string';

// =============================================================================
// ${fileName}
// =============================================================================
//
// ${fileDescription}
//
// @author ${author}
// @since ${date}
// =============================================================================
```

## Function Documentation
```scss
/// ${functionDescription}
/// 
/// @param {${paramType}} ${paramName} - ${paramDescription}
/// @returns {${returnType}} - ${returnDescription}
/// @throws {Error} ${errorDescription}
@function ${functionName}($${paramName}) {
  ${body}
}
```

## Mixin Documentation
```scss
/// ${mixinDescription}
/// 
/// @param {${paramType}} ${paramName} - ${paramDescription}
/// @content - ${contentDescription}
/// 
/// @returns {void} - ${returnDescription}
@mixin ${mixinName}($${paramName}) {
  ${body}
}
```

## Property Order
Properties should be ordered in the following groups:
1. Positioning (`position`, `top`, `right`, `bottom`, `left`, `z-index`)
2. Display & Box Model (`display`, `flex`, `grid`, `box-sizing`, `width`, `height`)
3. Spacing (`margin`, `padding`)
4. Border & Background (`border`, `border-radius`, `background`)
5. Typography (`color`, `font-*`, `text-*`, `line-height`)
6. Transitions & Animations
7. Other

## Naming Conventions
- Files: kebab-case with leading underscore (`_component-name.scss`)
- Variables: kebab-case with namespace (`$mono-color-primary`)
- Mixins/Functions: kebab-case (`@mixin create-grid`)
- Classes: BEM methodology (`block__element--modifier`)

## Best Practices
- Use triple-slash comments (`///`) for documentation
- Include parameter types and descriptions
- Document return values and side effects
- Group related properties together
- Use meaningful variable names
- Follow BEM naming convention for classes
- Avoid deep nesting (max 3 levels)
- Use relative units (rem, em) over pixels
- Leverage SASS features (variables, mixins, functions)
- Keep files focused and single-purpose
- Document magic numbers and important decisions

## Grid System
- Use the provided grid mixins for layout
- Follow the token-based approach for spacing
- Use responsive mixins for breakpoint handling
- Document grid-specific configurations

## Design Tokens
- Use token functions for values (`token()`, `slot()`)
- Follow the token hierarchy
- Document any custom token usage
- Use semantic token names

## Responsive Design
- Use the provided breakpoint mixins
- Follow mobile-first approach
- Document breakpoint-specific styles
- Use relative units for flexibility
